From d853cf8002745f8ad7c8c8357650f1ee28a5ac7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:19:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Fix the line: cover the whole avatar, avatar column only,
 Telegram groups only

- The line is now as wide as the avatars it hides (plus a little); the
  thickness setting is a minimum instead of the exact width.
- The avatar column is the median of the avatars inside the scrolling list, so
  a chat's header photo no longer pulls the line towards the toolbar.
- Telegram: inside a chat the line only appears in groups, recognised by a
  'members' header or a '168 members, 2 online' subtitle, with the position of
  the message bubbles as a fallback. Private chats and channels start their
  bubbles at the left edge, where the line used to cover them.
- Remove the per-scan 'rendering N avatar bars' log line.
